<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16854" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύφηλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>headstrong,</i> or perh.
				<i>foolish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς μ᾽ ἀσύφηλον ἐν Ἀργείοισιν
					ἔρεξεν ὡς εἴ τιν᾽ ἀτίμητον μετανάστην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.647
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ πω σεῦ ἄκουσα κακὸν ἔπος οὐδ᾽
					ἀσύφηλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.767
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				9.521
			</span></i>: also in late Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Eun.
				<u>VS</u>
				p.481B.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λως</span>”
				<i>foolishly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dius
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.21.16
			</span></i>.</div>
